TRANSCRIP-IT - DEVELOPMENT TRACKER
================================================================================

~- [EPIC] [TI-0001] Product discovery, scope, and delivery governance
  [DESC] Establish the approved Linux-first, local-first release baseline and maintain measurable phase gates.

    #- [ENH] [TI-0002] Convert the product plan into a structured development backlog
      [DESC] Organize the September 2026 plan into uniquely numbered epics and actionable tickets for review.
    ~- [ENH] [TI-0003] Approve the minimum viable product scope
      [DESC] Confirm the post-meeting Ubuntu workflow, supported English experience, and first-release boundaries.
    ~- [ENH] [TI-0004] Accept the deferred capability list
      [DESC] Confirm that live transcription, additional desktop platforms, bots, mobile capture, cloud collaboration, and calendar joining are deferred.
    ~- [ENH] [TI-0005] Select the working product name and repository location
    ~- [ENH] [TI-0006] Confirm the target Ubuntu audio environment
      [DESC] Record the Ubuntu version, audio server, microphone, headset, and meeting applications used for feasibility work.
    ~- [ENH] [TI-0007] Assemble a consented evaluation audio corpus
      [DESC] Collect 30 to 60 minutes covering actual accents, languages, speakers, noise, echo, interruptions, and microphone conditions.
    *- [ENH] [TI-0008] Record architecture and privacy decisions
    *- [ENH] [TI-0009] Operate one-week delivery iterations
      [DESC] Keep a prioritized backlog with acceptance criteria and demonstrate a usable vertical slice each week.
    *- [ENH] [TI-0010] Review scope, risk, benchmarks, and confidence at each phase gate

*- [EPIC] [TI-0011] Phase 0 audio, model, and privacy feasibility
  [DESC] Validate the platform-sensitive assumptions before investing in the production application.

    $- [FT] [TI-0012] Build an Ubuntu audio-capture feasibility spike
      [DESC] Provide consent-gated microphone and system-audio capture as exact, recoverable PCM WAV chunks with an atomic session manifest.
      [DESC] Testing found system playback in the microphone track; source routing or acoustic bleed must be diagnosed before approval.
      [DESC] Experimental offline adaptive filtering degraded voice clarity and must not be used as the production echo-cancellation path.
      [DESC] The replacement WebRTC mode preserves raw microphone audio, produces an echo-cancelled microphone track, and restores temporary playback routing after capture.
      [DESC] Accepted for the MVP with a headset recommendation and a warning that loud simultaneous system playback can suppress local speech.
    *- [ENH] [TI-0013] Verify separate and mixed audio tracks
      [DESC] Exercise microphone-only, system-audio-only, and combined capture paths.
      [DESC] Measure source readiness, establish a common session start, and verify track alignment after device wake-up.
    *- [ENH] [TI-0014] Benchmark two English transcription model sizes
      [DESC] Measure accuracy and speed across Indian accents, background noise, and domain terminology.
    *- [ENH] [TI-0015] Benchmark experimental multilingual transcription
      [DESC] Evaluate Malayalam, Hindi, Japanese, Manglish, Hinglish, and Japanese-English code-switching without making these results a release gate.
    *- [ENH] [TI-0016] Evaluate speaker-separation options
      [DESC] Compare licensing, downloads, runtime, hardware requirements, and labeling accuracy.
    ~- [ENH] [TI-0017] Select transcription, speaker, and summary strategies
      [DESC] Base model choices and realistic processing targets on measured Phase 0 results.
    *- [ENH] [TI-0018] Publish the feasibility report and benchmark results
    ~- [ENH] [TI-0019] Confirm measurable first-release acceptance criteria
      [DESC] Cover recording reliability, processing completion, transcript usability, summary grounding, privacy, and interruption recovery.

*- [EPIC] [TI-0020] Application foundation and recoverable job architecture
  [DESC] Establish the desktop shell, persistence, automated checks, and retry-safe processing foundation.

    $- [FT] [TI-0021] Create the repository structure and coding standards
      [DESC] Configure automated checks that run on every change.
      [DESC] Establish the repository layout, contribution rules, lockfile, continuous integration, and versioned pre-commit validation.
    $- [FT] [TI-0022] Build the Tauri, React, TypeScript, and Tailwind desktop shell
      [DESC] Provide a responsive local-first workspace shell, headset guidance, automated UI tests, and native Tauri continuous-integration checks.
      [DESC] Native Ubuntu testing found missing pkg-config and D-Bus development packages; retry after installing pkg-config and libdbus-1-dev.
      [DESC] Follow-up testing confirmed the main WebKitGTK, GTK, GLib, AppIndicator, SVG, Xdo, and OpenSSL development packages were not installed.
      [DESC] APT then exposed a disabled jammy-updates repository, leaving installed Pango runtime packages newer than the visible development packages.
      [DESC] Native Ubuntu launch, locked Rust compilation, frontend tests, and the production web build passed after restoring the standard development packages.
    $- [FT] [TI-0023] Add SQLite persistence and database migrations
      [DESC] Store meetings, transcript segments, jobs, actions, and settings.
      [DESC] Initialize bundled SQLite in the per-user application-data directory and apply ordered migrations transactionally.
      [DESC] Verified the live application database, migration idempotence, referential cleanup, integrity, Rust formatting, and warning-free Clippy output.
    $- [FT] [TI-0024] Implement the meeting lifecycle and job state machine
      [DESC] Persist lifecycle changes and make each processing step idempotent and safe to retry.
      [DESC] Guard meeting transitions with expected-state revisions and audit them using replay-safe idempotency keys.
      [DESC] Claim processing jobs with expiring lease tokens so stale workers cannot overwrite newer attempts.
      [DESC] Verified schema migration 2 against the live database, nine Rust state-machine tests, database integrity, and warning-free Clippy output.
    $- [ENH] [TI-0025] Separate original evidence from user and model-derived changes
      [DESC] Preserve source segments independently from corrections, translations, and generated interpretations.
      [DESC] Enforce immutable source text and append idempotent, provenance-tagged correction, translation, and romanization revisions.
      [DESC] Verified migration 3 against the live database, source-update rejection, revision selection, idempotent writes, and database integrity.
    *- [ENH] [TI-0026] Define replaceable engine interfaces
      [DESC] Allow engines to change without rewriting stored meeting data.
    *- [FT] [TI-0027] Support independently downloadable model packs
      [DESC] Keep the core installer small and offer Lite, Balanced, and Accuracy configurations.

*- [EPIC] [TI-0028] Meeting library and lifecycle management
  [DESC] Provide a clear local workspace for managing meetings throughout their lifecycle.

    *- [FT] [TI-0029] Create, rename, tag, archive, delete, and reopen meetings
    *- [FT] [TI-0030] Build the local meeting library
    *- [FT] [TI-0031] Require consent confirmation before recording
      [DESC] Show an unambiguous recording state and remind users of consent and policy responsibilities.
    *- [ENH] [TI-0032] Recover an interrupted meeting lifecycle on restart
      [DESC] Reopen unfinished recordings from the last safe checkpoint without corrupting completed work.

*- [EPIC] [TI-0033] Reliable microphone and system-audio capture
  [DESC] Capture meeting audio in recoverable chunks without silently losing data.

    *- [FT] [TI-0034] Select microphone and system-audio sources and capture modes
    *- [FT] [TI-0035] Implement start, pause, resume, and safe-stop controls
    *- [FT] [TI-0036] Display live audio levels and handle device changes
    *- [FT] [TI-0037] Write recoverable audio chunks and manifests
      [DESC] Flush progress periodically so forced termination preserves completed chunks.
    *- [ENH] [TI-0038] Prevent storage exhaustion during recording
      [DESC] Estimate required space, warn at live thresholds, and stop gracefully when necessary.
    *- [FT] [TI-0039] Play back separate captured tracks
      [DESC] The first iteration must capture and safely stop a ten-minute meeting, then play both tracks.
    *- [ENH] [TI-0040] Pass twenty controlled recording scenarios without lost audio
      [DESC] Cover long sessions, silence, disconnects, interruption, low disk space, cross-talk, and poor microphones.
    *- [ENH] [TI-0102] Improve echo cancellation during loud double-talk
      [DESC] Preserve local speech when the user and remote participant speak simultaneously or system playback is loud; address after the working MVP.

*- [EPIC] [TI-0041] Media import and preparation pipeline
  [DESC] Safely convert recordings and imported media into consistent, traceable processing inputs.

    *- [FT] [TI-0042] Import common audio and video files
    *- [FT] [TI-0043] Normalize, chunk, and detect speech in media
      [DESC] Use FFmpeg and retain metadata needed to trace outputs to the source timeline.
    *- [ENH] [TI-0044] Reject or safely handle malformed and malicious media
      [DESC] Surface actionable errors without compromising application data or the host system.

*- [EPIC] [TI-0045] Local transcription and speaker processing
  [DESC] Produce time-aligned English transcripts locally, with optional experimental language support.

    *- [FT] [TI-0046] Queue, monitor, cancel, retry, and resume processing jobs
    *- [FT] [TI-0047] Transcribe supported English speech with timestamps
      [DESC] Use a local Faster-Whisper adapter and make key statements understandable and time-aligned.
    *- [FT] [TI-0048] Offer an optional experimental multilingual pack
      [DESC] Preserve Malayalam, Hindi, Japanese, and mixed speech rather than forcing a meeting into English.
    *- [FT] [TI-0049] Show processing progress and recoverable errors
    *- [ENH] [TI-0050] Measure processing resource use on the target device
      [DESC] Track time, processor and memory use, temperature, and transcript usability.
    *- [FT] [TI-0051] Generate basic anonymous speaker labels
      [DESC] Do not infer identity silently; expose uncertainty when separation is unreliable.
    *- [FT] [TI-0052] Rename and merge speaker labels manually

*- [EPIC] [TI-0053] Evidence-preserving transcript review
  [DESC] Let users inspect and correct transcripts without overwriting the original evidence record.

    *- [FT] [TI-0054] View transcript timestamps and navigate to matching audio
    *- [FT] [TI-0055] Edit transcript text while preserving original segments
    *- [FT] [TI-0056] Regenerate only outputs affected by transcript corrections
    *- [ENH] [TI-0057] Mark low-confidence transcript segments visibly
      [DESC] Allow uncertain segments to be replayed, corrected, or reprocessed.
    *- [FT] [TI-0058] Choose native-script, romanized, or combined display
      [DESC] Display options must never overwrite the original transcript.

*- [EPIC] [TI-0059] Grounded summaries, decisions, and action tracking
  [DESC] Generate editable structured notes locally and make conclusions traceable to transcript evidence.

    *- [FT] [TI-0060] Define and validate the structured summary schema
      [DESC] Cover overview, topics, decisions, actions, questions, risks, and next steps.
    *- [FT] [TI-0061] Link generated decisions and actions to transcript evidence
      [DESC] Every generated fact must carry valid segment identifiers and timestamps or be visibly uncertain.
    *- [ENH] [TI-0062] Preserve unknown owners and dates as not specified
      [DESC] Reject unsupported claims instead of inventing details.
    *- [FT] [TI-0063] Run local structured generation through a replaceable model adapter
      [DESC] Start with Ollama and a quantized 3B to 4B model using constrained schemas and glossary support.
    *- [FT] [TI-0064] Edit, approve, and regenerate generated notes
      [DESC] Treat summaries as reviewable drafts rather than legally authoritative records.
    *- [FT] [TI-0065] Add meeting-specific summary templates
      [DESC] Include general discussion, daily stand-up, sprint review, and interview templates.
    *- [ENH] [TI-0066] Chunk long transcripts and synthesize grounded results
      [DESC] Analyze short or topic-based segments and retain structured facts with source timestamps.
    *- [FT] [TI-0067] Generate optional multilingual summaries and separate translations
      [DESC] Support selected summary languages while keeping interpretations separate from original evidence.

*- [EPIC] [TI-0068] Search and approved export
  [DESC] Make reviewed meeting knowledge easy to find and portable in open text formats.

    *- [FT] [TI-0069] Search transcript text with SQLite full-text search
    *- [FT] [TI-0070] Filter meetings by date, participant label, tag, and status
    *- [FT] [TI-0071] Export approved transcripts and notes to Markdown and plain text
    *- [ENH] [TI-0072] Retrieve relevant evidence for later meeting questions
      [DESC] Use matching segments instead of resending a complete transcript to the local model.

*- [EPIC] [TI-0073] Settings, diagnostics, and model operations
  [DESC] Expose understandable controls for local processing, storage, and troubleshooting.

    *- [FT] [TI-0074] Configure models, language, storage, retention, and privacy mode
    *- [FT] [TI-0075] Show diagnostics, storage usage, model status, and job errors
      [DESC] Diagnostic output must exclude transcript content and sensitive meeting data.
    *- [FT] [TI-0076] Guide first-run model installation and setup
    *- [ENH] [TI-0077] Verify downloaded model integrity
    *- [FT] [TI-0078] Back up and restore local meeting data

*- [EPIC] [TI-0079] Privacy, security, retention, and responsible use
  [DESC] Keep meeting content under owner control and document every data flow and optional connection.

    *- [FT] [TI-0080] Make fully local processing the default
      [DESC] Meeting content must not leave the device unless a future service is explicitly enabled.
    *- [ENH] [TI-0081] Encrypt sensitive stored content where practical
      [DESC] Protect encryption keys with the operating-system credential store.
    *- [ENH] [TI-0082] Exclude meeting content from logs and crash reports
    *- [FT] [TI-0083] Enforce retention limits and permanent deletion
      [DESC] Explain and verify removal of metadata, transcripts, and stored media.
    *- [ENH] [TI-0084] Review model and dependency licenses
      [DESC] Resolve distribution and commercial-use constraints before packaging.
    *- [ENH] [TI-0085] Verify local-only network behavior
      [DESC] Audit configuration and outbound traffic to prove meeting content remains on-device by default.

